            "evidence_span_id": "evidence-span:076e7ee6fee9bb080a0b17a1",
            "exact_text": "Second, the\nmethod strictly requires that every cell state contributing to a\ndoublet also be represented as a singlet state in the dataset. If\na particular singlet cell state is excluded experimentally, it trivially\ncannot be detected as part of a multiplet state, because the\nmissing parent state does not contribute to the simulated\ndoublet pool used for doublet classiﬁcation.",
